From: XXRI OS Team
Subject: [PATCH] qtwebengine: accept ffmpeg's x86-32 text relocations with GNU ld

FFmpeg's hand-written x86-32 assembly is not position independent
(x86inc.asm ignores PIC on x86-32, https://trac.ffmpeg.org/ticket/7878),
so objects like dct32.o carry text relocations. Chromium accepts them
on purpose and passes -Wl,-z,notext, but only for lld, on the premise
that GNU ld allows them silently. GNU ld warns ("creating DT_TEXTREL in
a shared object") and Chromium's -Wl,--fatal-warnings makes that fatal
when QtWebEngineCore is linked as a shared library on i386. Apply the
existing fix_textrels config for every x86-32 linker instead of turning
all fatal linker warnings off. The dynamic loader resolves the text
relocations at load time; the affected ffmpeg code pages are private
copies per process.
---
diff -ruN a/qtwebengine/src/3rdparty/chromium/third_party/ffmpeg/BUILD.gn b/qtwebengine/src/3rdparty/chromium/third_party/ffmpeg/BUILD.gn
--- a/qtwebengine/src/3rdparty/chromium/third_party/ffmpeg/BUILD.gn
+++ b/qtwebengine/src/3rdparty/chromium/third_party/ffmpeg/BUILD.gn
@@ -21,8 +21,9 @@
 
   # x86inc.asm ignores the PIC flag when compiling for x86 which unfortunately
   # causes text relocations in the object files generated by the assembler. We
-  # must disable the warning to allow linking with lld. Unlike gold, ld which
-  # will silently allow text relocations, lld support must be explicit.
+  # must disable the warning to allow linking with lld. GNU ld (bfd) also
+  # warns about them, and -Wl,--fatal-warnings turns that warning into an
+  # error, so it needs the same explicit permission; only gold is silent.
   #
   # See https://crbug.com/911658#c19 for more information. Tracked upstream at
   # https://trac.ffmpeg.org/ticket/7878
@@ -69,7 +70,7 @@
     }
 
     # See comments on fix_textrels config.
-    if (use_lld && current_cpu == "x86" && !is_win) {
+    if (current_cpu == "x86" && !is_win) {
       all_dependent_configs = [ ":fix_textrels" ]
     }
   }
